7T10:42:24Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: v4.5.stable.official [876b29033] ,v4.4.1.stable.official [49a5bc7b6]\n- Do not reproducible in: i don't have time for checking this one\n\n### System information\n\nArch Linux, Gnome DE - v4.5.stable.official [876b29033] - Vulkan 1.4.321 (Forward+) - 11th Gen Intel i3-1115G4 (4) @ 4.100GHz \n\n### Issue description\n\nIf you try to change the text of the Label node through a custom function by calling this function in another node, making the node where this function is in another node global, then the old text will remain along with the new one.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Make a main control node scene with a button as a child\n2. Make another control scene but with label in it(also make sure that there is text in label)\n3. Make that one scene with label global\n4. Put scene with label in scene with button\n5. Create script attached to the scene with label\n6. In that script write code with custom function that changes text property of label to something else\n7. Create script attached to the button\n8. Connect signal \"pressed\" to custom function that calls custom function in scene with label\n9. Now when you press button the new text appear on top of label, while old text is still here\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[runtime-change-text-bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22377183/runtime-change-text-bug.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.gi